current flow

Python is executing
       ↓
Something unexpected happens
       ↓
Exception occurs
       ↓
Program stops

----------------------------

For example :

Check 100 servers
      ↓
Server 1 → OK
Server 2 → OK
Server 3 → OK
Server 4 → missing data
      ↓
💥 Script crashes
      ↓
Servers 5–100 never get checked

---------------------------------

Handle the problem
---------------------

Check 100 servers
      ↓
Server 4 → problem
      ↓
Handle the problem
      ↓
Continue
      ↓
Server 5 → OK
Server 6 → OK
...

Syntax
--------
try:
    # code that might fail

except:
    # what to do if it fails

    situation           try         Except  else
| ---------------- | --------- | -------- | ------ |
| No exception     | ✅        | ❌        | ✅  |
| Exception occurs | Partially | ✅        | ❌    |

# Try → attempt operation
# Except → handle failure
# Else → operation succeeded
# finally → execute no matter what happens

